       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's about twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen.\n\n- **Order as written:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual ceiling for adults is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as up to 800 mg per dose. Over-the-counter use tops out at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. That's true even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg/day total, divided into some other schedule\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd also ask you to add a note with the clinical rationale."
