      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. I'm not aware of any indication that supports it. Each 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual 800 mg single-dose ceiling. At this level the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is substantial, and a higher dose won't give more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. I'm not willing to put in an order that is likely to harm the patient.\n\nThis isn't a judgment about your authority. If you have a specific rationale, such as a protocol or a unique clinical situation, here are two ways to proceed:\n- **Pharmacy:** Discuss it with the clinical pharmacist, who can review it and help with an override through the hospital's usual process.\n- **Different order:** I can enter a dose within the accepted range right now. For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the maximum. Or I can enter a lower dose if you tell me the indication.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
